    "description": "Self-indicating digital weighing indicators, mains or DC powered, designed to be used as part of Class III or IIII non-automatic weighing instruments. Available in desktop and wall-mounted versions. Devices: initial zero setting, semi-automatic zero setting, zero tracking, automatic zero setting (negative load indications for more than 5 s), semi-automatic subtractive tare weighing, preset tare, determination and indication of stability of equilibrium, zero indicator, MPP alibi storage device, up to 2 load receptors with summation, weighbridge modes (AdR/RDA, RcD, RpD), identification and recognition of the A/D converter of each weighing channel and of digital load cells / DILINK junction box (new calibration required if not recognised at power up), weight data transmission in open networks or wireless transmission in protected mode per Welmec 7.2 (encrypted; load receptor and indicator must be simultaneously visible), optional connection to external PC with printing from the MPP alibi storage device. Sealing: physical (protected switch) or software (password protection with non-resettable SW seal counter and change logging). Interfaces: load cell 6-wire shielded connection (analogue/digital), RS232/422/485, Ethernet, Wi-Fi (internal antenna), 0-10 V / 0-20 mA analogue input/output, digital I/O, field bus (Profibus...), USB host, SD card, audio."
